# MSBuild reads this file for every build under this directory, including the
# solution CMake generates in build/ -- which is what makes a plain
# `cmake --build build --config Release` build projects in parallel. Without
# it the Visual Studio generator runs MSBuild one project at a time unless
# --parallel is passed, and a grid.h edit rebuilt in 34 s instead of 8.
#
# -m with no count is one node per hardware thread. It multiplies with the /MP
# on the OBJECT libraries, bounded by their 24 files (see CMakeLists.txt).
-m
